# WARP Taskgen environment variables
# Copy to .env and fill in.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CLAUDE AUTH, pick ONE of the three methods below
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used by both (a) Claude Code inside Modal sandboxes for code exploration,
# profiling, and task generation, and (b) host-side Anthropic Messages API
# calls for Phase 2a/2b plus Phase 4 judges, classifiers, placement-fix,
# eval-awareness cue diagnosis, and eval-awareness rewrites.
#
# The two execution paths have different precedence. Modal Claude Code prefers
# OAuth first, then proxy auth, then direct API key. Host-side Messages API calls
# prefer proxy auth, then OAuth, then direct API key.
#
# 1) CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, Claude Pro / Max subscription auth.
#    Cheapest per call. Works with BOTH the Modal sandbox AND the host Messages
#    API (via Authorization: Bearer header; see phase_2_text_fill._call_anthropic_fallback).
#    If set, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL are NOT forwarded into
#    sandbox because OAuth does not route through a proxy.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=your_oauth_token_here
#
# 2) ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN + ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, OpenRouter or any proxy.
#    Put your OpenRouter key in ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (not ANTHROPIC_API_KEY),
#    set the base URL to https://openrouter.ai/api (no /v1 suffix), and leave
#    ANTHROPIC_API_KEY empty. Sandbox handles blanking ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
#    automatically when ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is set.
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-or-v1-...
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
#
# 3) ANTHROPIC_API_KEY alone, direct Anthropic API, billed per token.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here
#
# If CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN is set alongside ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, OAuth wins.
# Empty strings (e.g., ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="") are treated as unset by the host
# API path, matching the sandbox convention.
#
# GOTCHA, split credit pool between OPENROUTER_API_KEY and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN:
#   If your funded OpenRouter credit lives under OPENROUTER_API_KEY (the key
#   Browser-Use reads, below) but ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN is set to a DIFFERENT
#   (possibly depleted) OpenRouter token, the auth precedence above will pick
#   ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN and the Phase 4 judge/variant API calls will 402.
#   Three ways to fix:
#     (a) Alias the funded key before running:
#           export ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN="$OPENROUTER_API_KEY"
#     (b) Top up the ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN token's credits.
#     (c) Clear ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (and ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL) so OAuth or
#         ANTHROPIC_API_KEY takes over.
#   Phase 4 now pre-flights the API before running any task, a bad credential
#   fails at startup cost ~$0.0001 instead of after Browser-Use burns eval cost.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL AUTHENTICATION
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How YOU authenticate against Modal to create sandboxes. Easiest path:
# `modal token new` writes ~/.modal.toml. For CI/containers, set these:
# MODAL_TOKEN_ID=ak-...
# MODAL_TOKEN_SECRET=as-...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODAL NAMED-SECRET OVERRIDE (opt-in, CI-friendly)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If you have a curated Modal secret in a shared workspace, set its name
# here and WARP Taskgen will use Secret.from_name(<value>) instead of packaging
# your local shell env vars. The OAuth-wins fixup above does NOT apply in
# this mode. Whatever env vars the named secret contains are injected
# as-is, so managing them is your responsibility.
#
# Create one with e.g.:
#   modal secret create my-claude-secret CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=claude-...
#
# Then:
# WARP_TASKGEN_CLAUDE_MODAL_SECRET=my-claude-secret
# Legacy compatibility alias:
# WORLDSIM_CLAUDE_MODAL_SECRET=my-claude-secret

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER USE, evaluation agent LLM for Phase 4
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser Use runs locally, not in Modal. Its LLM provider is configured by
# Phase 4 CLI flags and BrowserUseAgent. These keys are local-only and are not
# forwarded into Modal sandboxes.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WEBARENA BENCHMARK INSTANCES, Phase 2c and Phase 4
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The user stands up WebArena instances per the WARP Taskgen spec
# "Prerequisites" section and supplies them to the orchestrator via CLI config.
# These placeholders are just a convenience for editing instance configs.
# Phase 2c and Phase 4 use GitLab/Reddit UGC carriers in the current mainline.
# Reddit/Postmill form/editor seeding typically reads this auto-login header:
# WARP_TASKGEN_REDDIT_AUTO_LOGIN=<postmill-username>:<postmill-password>
#
# GitLab editor calls normally use API auth/PAT config and Phase 0d-minted
# storage_state for agent login.
#
# Keep db_connection concrete in instances.json. Do not use env interpolation
# for DB URIs. Typical current WebArena Verified examples:
# - gitlab: postgresql://gitlab:...@HOST:5432/gitlabhq_production
# - reddit: postgresql://postmill:postmill@HOST:5432/postmill
# Shopping, shopping_admin, map/OSM, Magento, Wikipedia, and classifieds are
# historical full-benchmark/support plumbing unless the spec reopens scope.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Override where pipeline state and artifacts are written (default: ./logs/).
# WARP_TASKGEN_STATE_DIR=logs
# Legacy compatibility alias:
# WORLDSIM_STATE_DIR=logs

# Phase 4 PVPO: each execution instance should carry its own `pvpo_cdp_url`
# in the instances file. Shipping r5 runs use dedicated chrome-headless-shell
# Docker containers, one CDP endpoint per worker. The old single
# WORLDSIM_PVPO_CDP_URL override is legacy and should not be used for rigor
# runs.

# Override the WebArena Verified evaluator Python. Default is the
# repo-relative packages/warp-taskgen-webarena-verified/.venv/bin/python
# resolved via worldsim/_paths.find_repo_root (sentinel-walk).
# WARP_TASKGEN_WEBARENA_EVAL_PYTHON=./packages/warp-taskgen-webarena-verified/.venv/bin/python

# Opt non-WebArena-Verified benchmarks into runtime storage_state auto-heal.
# For WebArena Verified this defaults to true (dummy creds already in repo).
# WORLDSIM_AUTO_MINT_STORAGE_STATE=false
